The original loop re-evaluates `fields.size()` and converts to `int` on every iteration, and indexes through `operator[]`. The rewrite walks a raw pointer range over the vector's storage instead, which keeps the same first-match semantics and return values. It adds no members or state.

```cpp
Field* Mesg::GetField(const FIT_UINT8 fieldNum)
{
    Field* const begin = fields.data();
    Field* const end = begin + fields.size();
    for (Field* f = begin; f != end; ++f)
    {
        if (f->GetNum() == fieldNum)
            return f;
    }

    return FIT_NULL;
}
```